          %title Supersymmetry
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %blockquote
            %p
              this entry is one section of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry+and+superphysics"}> geometry of physics – supergeometry and superphysics
              ” which is one chapter of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"}> geometry of physics
              ”
            %p
              previous section:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} geometry of physics – supergeometry
            %p
              next section
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In the broad sense of the word a
            %em super-symmetry
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            is an action of some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            the term is used more specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} extend
            some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            symmetry group, and for their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            content of some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
          %p
            If, by default, spacetime is locally modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (of some dimension) whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            in this dimension, then
            %em supersymmetry
            in the strict sense of the word is super-extension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            whose odd-graded component is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+representation"}> Majorana representation
            ”) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            in the given dimension. The result is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            for the given spacetime dimension and choice of real spin representation, the latter also being called the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+of+supersymmetries"}> number of supersymmetries
            ”.
          %p
            Just as – in the spirit of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            – one recovers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            by the
            = succeed "-cover" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            defines
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            is then a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            locally modeled on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature. But other local model spacetimes may be used, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+anti-de+Sitter+spacetimes"} super anti-de Sitter spacetimes
            etc.
          %p
            Just as ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            are usefully studied via their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+groups"} super Lie groups
            are conveniently studied via their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extensions"} Lie algebra extensions
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistors"} twistors
            or the positivity relations that enter the spinorial proof of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+theorem"} positive energy theorem
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 20px 10px 20px;"}
            %img{:alt => "The Fano place", :src => "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Fano_plane.svg/330px-Fano_plane.svg.png", :title => "A picture of the Fano plane", :width => "360"}/
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
            have a comparatively rigid classification, there are algebraic constraints on supersymmetry groups in various dimensions. By a remarkable algebraic coincidence, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representations"} real spin representations
            in spacetime dimensions 3,4,5,6,7,10, and 11 are given by simple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            over the real
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            (
            %a{:href => "#KugoTownsend82"}> Kugo-Townsend 82
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sudbery84"} Sudbery 84
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezHuerta10"} Baez-Huerta 10
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fano+plane"} Fano plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            and fundamental structures in mathematics (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"}> stable homotopy theory
            ) where these algebras, and their associated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+fibrations"} Hopf fibrations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
            theorem and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
          %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/TheSpacetimeExtensions.png", :width => "250"}/
          %p
            Conversely, it turns out (theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperpointMaximalInvariantCentralExtensions"}
            below) that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            in these dimensions are characterized as being the iterated maximal invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            (
            %a{:href => "#MTheoryFromTheSuperpoint"}> Huerta-Schreiber 17
            ). This shows that supersymmetry in the special sense of spacetime supersymmetry is mathematically singled out among all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            themselves are mathematically singled out by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"} Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            is not an ad-hoc concept and is of intrinsic interest independently of debated speculations on its realization at the (comparatively “low”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electroweak+symmetry+breaking"} electroweak energy scale
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
          %p
            (In fact
            %a{:href => "supersymmetry#ClassificationSuperconformal"} superconformal symmetry
            has an even more rigid classification: it exists only in dimensions 3, 4, 5, and 6, where it turns out to form the local super-symmetry groups appearing in the
            = succeed ".)" do
