              \.
          %p
            Using the properties of real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
            thus established, it is then immediate to construct spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Supersymmetry"} Spacetime supersymmetry
          %p Finally we discuss that instead of pre-describing bosonic spacetime symmetry and then asking for super-extensions of it, one may discover spacetime, spin geometry and supersymmetry all at once by a systematic mathematical process starting from just the superpoint:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#SupersymmetryFromTheSuperpoint"} Supersymmetry from the superpoint
          %h2#SuperExtensionOfPoincareLieAlgebra Supersymmetry extensions
          %p
