              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebras"} super Poincaré Lie algebras
              at least in certain dimensions are singled out from a different perspective: they are precisely the result of iterative maximal invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
              of the superpoint.
          %h2#RealSpinRepresentations Real spin representations
          %p
            By example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperExtensionOfPoincare"}
            we want a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
            in order to construct a spacetime supersymmetry super Lie algebra. There are different ways to get hold of real spin representations.
          %p
            One way is to first consider complex representations, which are easy to come by, and then try to carve out real sub-representations inside them by finding a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
            on the representation. In physics this is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            construction. This we discuss in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#MajoranaSpinors"} Real spinors as Majorana spinors
          %p
            Another way to get real spin representations is to invoke some algebraic magic that allows to construct them right away. This turns out to work in spacetime dimensions 3,4,6 and 10 as well as 4,5,7 and 11 by considering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \times 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in one of the four real
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternative+algebra"} alternative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras"} division algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#RealSpinRepresentationViaNormedDivisionAlgebra"} Real spinors via Real alternative division algebras
              \.
          %h3#MajoranaSpinors Real spinors as Majorana spinors
          %p We will discuss the following concept, the ingredients of which we explain in the following
          #MajoranaSpinorGeneral.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
